# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The Dockerfile does `COPY aml/ ./aml/`. Several files in
# aml/ are local A/B harnesses that embed a live answer-model API key and a local
# SOCKS proxy address. They are gitignored, so a build from a public GitHub clone
# never sees them — but a build from a working checkout would bake the key into an
# image layer, where it survives even if a later layer deletes the file. This list
# makes the image safe to build from either context.
#
# Rule of thumb: anything that is not needed to serve POST /add and POST /search
# stays out of the image.

# Credentials and local provider config — never image material.
.pi-memory/
embed-provider.json
models.json
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# Local A/B harnesses, validators and their outputs (embed keys + benchmark answers).
aml/ab-*.ts
aml/test-multi.ts
aml/bench-local.ts
aml/run-validation.*
aml/results-*
aml/*.log
aml/*.jsonl
aml/*.cmd
aml/*.ps1
validation.pid
temporal-ab.flag
tl-harm.flag

# Benchmarks, corpora and internal analysis — large and not part of the service.
bench/
prd/
docs/
architecture/
test/
AGENTS.md

# Large local embedding models and caches.
models/
*.onnx

# Dependencies and VCS — the image installs deps itself.
node_modules/
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Build output and OS/IDE noise.
dist/
build/
tmp/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
